1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:04,450
Did you notice how nature sometimes repeats itself?
你有没有注意到，大自然中的事物有时会重复出现？

2
00:00:05,250 --> 00:00:07,470
Something that repeats is called a pattern.
重复出现的事物就叫作规律。

3
00:00:08,270 --> 00:00:10,720
There are many patterns for you to study and learn.
有很多规律可供你研究和学习。

4
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:12,590
Look around you.
看看你的四周吧。

5
00:00:13,390 --> 00:00:14,730
Patterns are everywhere.
规律无处不在。

6
00:00:15,530 --> 00:00:19,200
You may see bright and colorful patterns if you look at fish in the sea.
如果看看海里的鱼，你可能会看到鲜艳多彩的图案。

7
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,240
In a bee’s honeycomb, the six-sided shape is repeated many times.
在蜜蜂的蜂巢里，六边形重复出现了许多次。

8
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:27,420
Some leaves always have five points on them.
有些叶子上总是有五个尖。

9
00:00:28,220 --> 00:00:31,300
Listening carefully, you will find a noisy world.
仔细听一听，你会发现这个世界很嘈杂。

10
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:35,250
Dogs bark, the rain falls and the wind blows.
狗在叫，雨在下，风在吹。

11
00:00:36,050 --> 00:00:37,250
Are these patterns?
这些是规律吗？

12
00:00:38,050 --> 00:00:38,890
Of course!
当然是！

13
00:00:39,690 --> 00:00:41,500
Sounds that repeat are patterns.
重复出现的声音就是规律。

14
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:45,860
A cricket uses its wings to make repeated chirping sounds.
蟋蟀用翅膀反复发出啁啾叫声。

15
00:00:46,660 --> 00:00:49,570
Do you know that a cricket’s chirp changes with the temperature?
你知道蟋蟀的啁啾叫声会随着温度变化吗？

16
00:00:50,370 --> 00:00:53,640
The hotter it is, the more chirps a cricket will make.
天气越热，蟋蟀叫的次数就越多。

17
00:00:54,440 --> 00:00:57,020
Try to find out how living things grow around you.
试着弄清楚你身边的生物是怎样生长的。

18
00:00:57,820 --> 00:00:59,270
Seeds grow into plants.
种子会长成植物。

19
00:01:00,070 --> 00:01:02,210
A butterfly begins life as an egg.
蝴蝶的生命是从一颗卵开始的。

20
00:01:03,010 --> 00:01:05,680
Each living thing has its own pattern as it grows.
每种生物在生长过程中都有自己的规律。

21
00:01:06,480 --> 00:01:09,290
When a human baby is born, it is small.
人类的婴儿出生时很小。

22
00:01:10,090 --> 00:01:14,380
With time, the baby learns to lift its head and learns to roll over.
随着时间推移，婴儿学会了抬头，也学会了翻身。

23
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:17,680
Finally, the baby learns to stand up and walk.
最后，婴儿学会了站立和走路。

24
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:21,430
This kind of pattern is called a pattern of development.
这种规律叫作发育规律。

25
00:01:22,230 --> 00:01:26,730
If something happens over and over, it, too, forms a pattern.
如果某件事一再发生，那么它也会形成一种规律。

26
00:01:27,530 --> 00:01:31,170
For example, you get up at 7:00 every morning.
比如，你每天早上7:00起床。

27
00:01:31,970 --> 00:01:35,130
You get dressed and then eat breakfast at 7:30 a.m.
你穿好衣服，然后在早上7:30吃早饭。

28
00:01:35,930 --> 00:01:39,300
If you repeat this many times, it becomes a pattern.
如果你多次重复这个过程，它就成了一种规律。

29
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:43,060
Having a music class every Monday is a pattern.
每周一上音乐课是一种规律。

30
00:01:43,860 --> 00:01:48,140
So is going to school five days a week and having Saturday and Sunday off.
每周上五天学、周六和周日休息，也是一种规律。

31
00:01:48,940 --> 00:01:51,550
It seems as if the world is full of patterns.
世界似乎充满了规律。

32
00:01:52,350 --> 00:01:56,850
Just think—without patterns, the world would be much harder to study!
想想看，要是没有规律，这个世界研究起来就会难得多！
